Dialogue: 0,0:05:42.44,0:05:45.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}In south London, two water companies ran their pipes
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.69,0:05:47.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}down the same streets.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.07,0:05:50.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}In 1852, the Lambeth Company moved its intake up the
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.32,0:05:53.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}Thames, to Thames Ditton, getting water free of
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.26,0:05:54.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}London's sewage.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.26,0:05:57.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}The Southwark and Vauxhall Company still drew from
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.39,0:05:58.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(80,80)}the Thames at Battersea.
